module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.non_empty_append_on_a_persistent_vector_is_superlinear

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data non_empty_append_on_a_persistent_vector_is_superlinear: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "non_empty_append_on_a_persistent_vector_is_superlinear" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "rc_list_concat appends a small right side element by element and keeps im Vector append for large right sides, with the threshold measured, SUFFICIENT FOR gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder concat_chain to double linearly on the emitted path, and a control that times that arm across doublings and goes red when the ratio leaves the linear band."
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a sequence built by repeatedly appending a small right side onto a growing left side costs more than linear time in the number of appends. std.algebra non_empty_append realizes its tail as list_append(list_snoc_item(left.tail, right.head), right.tail), and list_append lowers to v1_rt rc_list_concat, which is make_mut(a).append(b.clone()) on an im Vector (v1.compiler.runtime_rust rt_rc_container_ops).",
    "HARM: an accumulator over FreeMonoid or FreeSemigroup pays a cost that grows faster than its length, on the emitted Rust path and in the v1 interpreter. Fold accumulators already call non_empty_append on non-text sequences (std.generated_provider group_provider_demands, gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge runner_host_cap_pending_reloads, gunbc.host.host_converge slice_control_plan_of), so far on small n. The A4(a) NonEmptyStr cut would route every migrated text accumulator through the same append, so the defect blocks that cut (operator ruling 2026-10-23: no cut and no generator until the cause is found and fixed).",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, AND WHICH PART EACH SOURCE ESTABLISHES. The arms are gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder, one per link. The label //gunbc/instruments:append-chain-ladder (gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder_native) builds each arm at n = 2000, 4000, 8000 and 16000 on the emitted path, checks the element count it owes, times it best-of-5, and judges each doubling with ladder_linearity (see the CONTROL and EXECUTED rows). The CURVE below was first read by an out-of-band timing run on srv1, 2026-10-23, not by the label: the main seed at 08437488ec1 (bin 0d1af18c) emitted the arms to Rust, each was timed best-of-5 over doubling n from 2000 to 32000 in one build-and-run dispatch, and gunbc run timed the interpreter arms from 1000 to 8000 or 16000. The timing rows and their ratio-threshold fold landed with the rc_list_concat fix, so the label now re-derives the curve's linearity; the srv1 ratios below stay a transcribed reading of that run. push_chain (list_snoc_item alone) doubles linearly. concat_chain (list_append alone, fixed 8-element right side) does not: its ratio per doubling rises toward 4. elementwise_chain (the same right side appended one element at a time) doubles linearly. non_empty_append_chain follows concat_chain. The same split holds on the emitted path and in the interpreter. concat_chain and elementwise_chain append the same 8-element right side, through list_append and through one list_snoc_item per element. One is superlinear and the other linear, so the growth is carried by the list_append realization, rc_list_concat over im::Vector::append. The mechanism inside it is not isolated: the two arms also differ in their make_mut and clone pattern, so this row makes no claim about aliasing or make_mut.",
    "CAUSE, MEASURED NOT EXPLAINED: the earliest unjustified boundary is rc_list_concat, which realizes every append, including a small right side onto a large left, as im Vector append. The mechanism inside im is not examined; the concat_chain / elementwise_chain pair locates the growth in the list_append realization (rc_list_concat over im::Vector::append), not which part of it. The interpreter realizes list_append through its own route and shows the same curve; under the v1 freeze that path gets no performance work and is recorded here only.",
    "THE REPAIR AND ITS THRESHOLD (sunny-bee-153, stacked on PR #14751): v1.compiler.runtime_rust rc_list_concat pushes a right side of at most LIST_CONCAT_ELEMENTWISE_MAX = 4096 elements one at a time (the one append rule, append_persistent, which list_concat now shares) and keeps im Vector append above it. The threshold is a measured crossover, not a guess: a one-off bench on the remote amd64 runner, 2026-10-24, im 15.1.0, best of 3, chained appends of a k-element right side, read push time over append time 0.60 to 0.72 at k = 3584 and 4096, 0.94 to 1.06 at 4352, and 0.98 to 1.31 from 4608 up, rising to 2.36 to 3.09 at 16384. The crossing is a sharp step between 4096 and 4352, so 4096 is the largest measured k where element-wise push wins at every step count. That bench is a reading, not an instrument; the label below re-derives the curve the fix must hold, not the crossover.",
    "THE CONTROL: //gunbc/instruments:append-chain-ladder now runs the arms on the EMITTED path (gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder_native through NativeClaimProgramProducer), times each (arm, n) best of 5 at n = 2000, 4000, 8000 and 16000, and judges every doubling with gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder ladder_linearity: held 0, superlinear 1, no readable curve 2. The 2.5x-per-doubling band is a POLICY BUDGET (a linear arm read about 2.0 and the pre-fix append 2.1 to 3.6), not a measured constant. The label is NOT on the required path, so this is mechanical prevention only where someone runs it.",
    "EXECUTED, 2026-10-24, remote amd64, one dispatch per arm pair: with the fix, `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:append-chain-ladder` exited 0 with all four arms linear; with ONLY the stage0 runtime mirror reverted to im Vector append (the RED), it exited 1 with concat_chain at 256/100 and non_empty_append_chain at 253/100 per doubling from n = 2000 while push_chain and elementwise_chain stayed linear. The rung stays Mitigatable: the label is not on the required path, so the control does not reliably execute.",
    "CEILING: mechanically preventable, through a control that times concat_chain across doublings. Construction is not available: the carrier admits the append, and its cost is a property of the realization. The label observes append cost and goes red when the fix is reverted (EXECUTED row), but no REQUIRED control does: nothing in v2-bootstrap runs the label, so a revert leaves every required check green. That is why the rung stays mitigatable.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.runtime_rust", decl_name: "rt_rc_container_ops"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "non_empty_append"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "list_append"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "push_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "concat_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "elementwise_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.append_chain_ladder", decl_name: "non_empty_append_chain"),
  ],
}
